: "[P2] fresh-machine `--user --seccomp` fails on any 0700-home host: seccomp loader unreadable under the mapped launch (bunker install leg, live repro)", "priority": "P1", "detail": "2026-09-23 dogfood, fresh Debian 13 bunker agent 3c18196b (destroyed), HEAD b0bd621, install 0s. `terminal-jail --user --seccomp <cmd>` — the exact quickstart §3c form — fails: python3: can't open file '~/.local/lib/terminal-jail/seccomp-loader.py': [Errno 13] Permission denied. Root cause chain: on a mapping-capable host --user takes the uid-mapped launch; the mapped payload runs as subordinate uid 231072; the agent home is mode 0700 (bunkerd default) so DAC denies traversal to ~/.local/lib/terminal-jail/ and python3 cannot exec the loader. Same failure via the repo checkout (app/standalone). Bare `--seccomp` (no --user) works on the same box (Seccomp: 2, filter denies mount mount-rc=32, pivot_root, keyctl EPERM). Host-control repro: this fleet control host (home 711) passes --user --seccomp (Seccomp: 2/1). FIX DIRECTION: ship the loader through a world-traversable install path (e.g. ~/.local/share/terminal-jail or a preflight that copies the loader to a traversable tmp dir before the mapped exec), or probe DAC-traversability of the loader path before taking the mapped launch and degrade with the loud warning the wrapper already uses for --user. Docs: quickstart §3c should note the 0700-home failure mode. Install smoke evidence: /tmp/dogfood-tj/bunker-smoke.sh transcript (host-local).", "created_at": "2026-09-23 04:55:00", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/terminal-jail-TJ-DF-019", "branch": "wt/TJ-DF-019", "sessions": ["terminal-jail-2026-09-23-13-46-44"]}
